resources.string:
"About
Supports LAN and Direct transfer modes; Direct is the default.
LAN mode: transfers data between devices on the same local network; stay close to the router for better speed.
Direct mode: the receiver connects to a hotspot created by the sender to transfer data.

Notes
If the sender and receiver use different protocol versions, the transfer may fail.
The sender should turn off Wi-Fi and Bluetooth for the hotspot to reach full speed.
Using the \"Power Save\" performance profile may reduce transfer speed.

Features
1. Direct read/write with no compression — less heat and no extra storage needed;
2. Verified by file size and SHA-256; pause and resume at any time;
3. On-demand transfer — only missing or changed files are sent;
4. One-tap migration and installation of game APKs and resource packs, with the directory structure faithfully restored;
5. You can leave this page at any time during the transfer;
6. Should support transferring apps whose data contains symlinks, such as Termux;"
